---
layout: base.njk
title: StylePort — CSS & UserCSS Manager for Safari on Mac
description: StylePort is a free, open-source CSS and UserCSS manager for Safari on Mac. Download the signed direct edition or join the public TestFlight beta.
---
<section class="hero shell">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Safari-first UserCSS manager</p>
    <h1>The web,<span>wearing your colors.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">Import plain CSS and UserCSS themes, tune their variables, and make the sites you use feel like yours—without handing over your browsing history.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="#download" data-tinylytics-event="cta.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="hero">Get StylePort <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#features" data-tinylytics-event="cta.features" data-tinylytics-event-value="hero">See what it does</a>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-row" aria-label="Product details">
      <span>macOS 14+</span><span>Free &amp; open source</span><span>No account</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-demo" aria-label="StylePort style manager preview">
    <div class="demo-topbar">
      <span class="traffic-lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="demo-address">Style manager · StylePort</span>
      <span class="demo-status">Local</span>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-body">
      <aside>
        <div class="demo-wordmark">STYLEPORT</div>
        <strong>Style library</strong>
        <span class="demo-search">Search styles</span>
        <span>＋ New style</span>
        <span class="demo-active">⇧ Import style</span>
        <small>Stored on this Mac</small>
      </aside>
      <div class="demo-content">
        <div class="demo-style-card">
          <span class="demo-check">✓</span>
          <div><strong>Midnight for Mastodon</strong><small>Enabled · 4 target sites</small></div>
          <span class="demo-pill">USERCSS</span>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-code" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>--accent: #8aadf4;</span><span>--surface: #181926;</span><span>--radius: 14px;</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="marquee" aria-label="StylePort capabilities">
  <div><span>PLAIN CSS</span><i>✦</i><span>USERCSS</span><i>✦</i><span>VARIABLES</span><i>✦</i><span>URL MATCHING</span><i>✦</i><span>BACKUPS</span><i>✦</i><span>UPDATES</span></div>
</section>

<section class="section shell" id="features">
  <div class="section-heading split-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">A proper home for your CSS</p><h2>Everything your styles need.</h2></div>
    <p>StylePort brings a proven UserCSS engine to Safari and reshapes the experience around clarity, reliability, and WebKit.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-mark">01</span><h3>Import without friction</h3><p>Choose a local .css or .user.css file, paste CSS directly, or review a style from a URL before installing it.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-mark">02</span><h3>Make themes yours</h3><p>Adjust colors, ranges, toggles, select menus, text, and image variables exposed by UserCSS themes.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-mark">03</span><h3>Apply precisely</h3><p>Match styles to domains, URLs, URL prefixes, and regular expressions with the mature Stylus matching engine.</p></article>
    <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-mark">04</span><h3>Keep control</h3><p>Enable, disable, edit, reorder, back up, restore, and update styles from one focused library.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section shell visual-section">
  <div class="product-shot"><img src="{{ '/press/import-style.png' | url }}?v={{ site.assetVersion }}" alt="StylePort import screen in Safari with file, URL, and pasted CSS choices" width="3448" height="2034" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
  <div class="visual-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">One import door</p><h2>File, URL, or paste. Your choice.</h2>
    <p>One deliberate import flow replaces scattered upload actions. Every style is reviewed before installation, whether it came from your Mac or a URL you supplied.</p>
    <ul class="check-list"><li><span>✓</span> Preview metadata before installing</li><li><span>✓</span> Give plain CSS a clear name</li><li><span>✓</span> Keep backup restore separate and explicit</li></ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="privacy-band">
  <div class="shell privacy-grid">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p><h2>Your browsing is not the product.</h2></div>
    <div class="privacy-points">
      <article><strong>Local storage</strong><p>Your styles and settings stay in Safari extension storage on your Mac.</p></article>
      <article><strong>No surveillance</strong><p>The app has no behavioral analytics, advertising, cross-app tracking, or StylePort account. Optional tips use purchase reporting only.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Explainable access</strong><p>Website permission is used only to match and apply the styles you choose.</p></article>
      <a href="{{ '/privacy/' | url }}" class="text-link">Read the complete privacy policy <span>→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section shell pricing-section" id="pricing">
  <div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Simple on purpose</p><h2>Free means the whole app.</h2><p>No subscription, no premium feature gate, and no separate plans to decode.</p></div>
  <div class="price-card">
    <div><span class="price-label">StylePort</span><div class="price">$0</div><p>For everyone, with every feature.</p></div>
    <ul class="check-list"><li><span>✓</span> Full UserCSS manager</li><li><span>✓</span> Free and open-source</li><li><span>✓</span> Optional support—never required</li></ul>
    <div class="support-note">
      <strong>Want to help?</strong>
      <p>Make a voluntary one-time contribution toward signing, hosting, testing, and continued development. Support never unlocks a different edition—the whole app stays free.</p>
      <a class="button support-button" href="{{ site.supportUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="support.checkout" data-tinylytics-event-value="stripe">Support StylePort <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="download-section" id="download">
  <div class="shell download-grid">
    {% if directRelease.available %}
    <div><p class="eyebrow">StylePort for Safari</p><h2>Choose how you get StylePort.</h2><p>The RelayByte direct edition is available now. Apple’s public TestFlight beta remains open, while the Mac App Store edition is coming soon. Every channel keeps the complete app free.</p></div>
    <div class="release-channels">
      <article class="release-channel direct-channel" aria-labelledby="direct-channel-title">
        <div class="channel-heading"><span class="channel-label">Direct from RelayByte</span><span class="channel-status available">Available now</span></div>
        <div class="channel-product"><img src="{{ '/brand/styleport/app/styleport-app-128.png' | url }}" alt="StylePort app icon" width="64" height="64"><div><h3 id="direct-channel-title">StylePort {{ directRelease.version }}</h3><p>Build {{ directRelease.build }} · macOS {{ directRelease.minimumSystemVersion }}+</p></div></div>
        <p>Download the exact Developer ID–signed and Apple-notarized release. The direct edition uses StylePort’s signed Sparkle feed for updates and always asks before installing.</p>
        <a class="button channel-button" href="{{ directRelease.archivePath | url }}" download data-tinylytics-event="app.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="relaybyte-direct">Download signed ZIP <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <details class="release-integrity"><summary>Release files and verification</summary><code>{{ directRelease.archiveSha256 }}</code><div class="download-links"><a href="{{ directRelease.releaseNotesPath | url }}">Release notes</a><a href="{{ directRelease.checksumPath | url }}" download data-tinylytics-event="file.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="styleport-direct-checksum">ZIP checksum</a><a href="{{ directRelease.sourcePath | url }}" download data-tinylytics-event="file.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="styleport-gpl-source">GPL source</a><a href="{{ directRelease.sourceChecksumPath | url }}" download data-tinylytics-event="file.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="styleport-source-checksum">Source checksum</a><a href="{{ '/updates/appcast.xml' | url }}">Signed update feed</a></div></details>
      </article>
      <article class="release-channel apple-channel" aria-labelledby="apple-channel-title">
        <div class="channel-heading"><span class="channel-label">Through Apple</span><span class="channel-status beta">Beta open</span></div>
        <div class="channel-product"><img src="{{ '/brand/styleport/app/styleport-app-128.png' | url }}" alt="StylePort app icon" width="64" height="64"><div><h3 id="apple-channel-title">Apple distribution</h3><p>macOS 14+ · Updates delivered by Apple</p></div></div>
        <div class="apple-choice"><div><strong>TestFlight beta</strong><span>Available now</span><p>Try the Apple-distributed beta and help test StylePort before its App Store release.</p><a class="button channel-button" href="{{ site.testFlightUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="app.testflight" data-tinylytics-event-value="testflight-beta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join TestFlight <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div><strong>Mac App Store</strong>{% if site.appStoreUrl %}<span>Available now</span><p>Download the Apple-distributed release from the Mac App Store.</p><a class="button channel-button" href="{{ site.appStoreUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="app.appstore" data-tinylytics-event-value="mac-app-store" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on Mac App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% else %}<span>Coming soon</span><p>The App Store edition is not public yet. There is no store badge or purchase link until Apple’s release is live.</p>{% endif %}</div></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Public TestFlight beta</p><h2>Help test StylePort in Safari.</h2><p>StylePort is still in development. Join the public TestFlight beta on a Mac running macOS 14 or later to try version 1.0 and help uncover issues before release.</p></div>
    <div class="download-card">
      <img src="{{ '/brand/styleport/app/styleport-app-128.png' | url }}" alt="StylePort app icon" width="64" height="64">
      <div><strong>StylePort Beta</strong><span>Safari on Mac · macOS 14+</span></div>
      <a class="button beta-button" href="{{ site.testFlightUrl }}" data-tinylytics-event="app.testflight" data-tinylytics-event-value="testflight-beta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join TestFlight <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <p class="download-note">Beta software may contain bugs. A direct download is not available yet.</p>
      <a class="download-roadmap" href="{{ '/roadmap/' | url }}">View the roadmap →</a>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
